2858:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** /*********************************************************************
2859:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2860:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *       SEGGER_SYSVIEW_EncodeId()
2861:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2862:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Function description
2863:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Encode a 32-bit Id in shrunken variable-length format.
2864:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2865:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Parameters
2866:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    pPayload - Pointer to where the Id will be encoded.
2867:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Id       - The 32-bit value to be encoded.
2868:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2869:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Return value
2870:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Pointer to the byte following the value, i.e. the first free
2871:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    byte in the payload and the next position to store payload
2872:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    content.
2873:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2874:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Additional information
2875:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    The parameters to shrink an Id can be configured in
2876:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    SEGGER_SYSVIEW_Conf.h and via SEGGER_SYSVIEW_SetRAMBase().
2877:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *     SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_BASE: Lowest Id reported by the application.
